      "writtenOn": "2023-08-03T05:29:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think the problem is deeper in status.go.  The metrics are not written until after `stat.Finish()` has been called, which is documented as:\n```\n// Finish will call Flush on all the outputs, generally flushing or closing all\n// of their outputs. Do not call any other functions on this instance or any\n// associated ToolStatus instances after this has been called.\n```\n\nBut nothing from status.go calls tells the ninja reader goroutine to stop sending data, so if ninja is still running it will happily call the `ToolStatus` methods.  I think when `Finish()` is called it needs to either signal the `ToolStatus` inputs to tell them to stop sending data, or to ignore any further data sent from `ToolStatus` inputs.",
      "parentUuid": "b8a0e503_c4e4f19b",
      "revId": "5d63ad61ba501ae4b3659336a70dfb2a10769f10",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
